Meta-State Flags: #ATOMIC #FINALE #DECLERATION
This specification defines the Kubernetes and Terraform server-to-server validation, identity verification (receiving URL or URI), and state transition protocol for ALL systems within the METAVERSE, OMNIVERSE, IOT, and IOS architectures, spanning all DOMAINS AND IPs—specifically expanding cross-network ingestion to encapsulate NASA and AARO Military tactical data networks for secure UAP (Unidentified Anomalous Phenomena) document localization, extraction, and deep payload encapsulation.
1. Protocol Overview
The ECH Dap Up is a zero-trust, high-velocity mutual authentication and state migration mechanism. It replaces legacy TCP/TLS multi-roundtrip handshakes with an atomic, single-sequence Handshake + Handoff flow utilizing universal <*/AUTH*> wildcards to establish instant Sovereign Parity between infrastructure nodes.
 * Handshake (The Contact): Cryptographic mutual identification over raw IP rails, fortified via hidden tracers in the payload whitespace and secure state cookies.
 * Handoff (The Release & Extraction): Immediate transfer of ledger state, execution tokens, or session authority. When interfacing with aerospace or military nodes (NASA/AARO), this phase handles the instantaneous localization, copy extraction, and cryptographic encapsulation of isolated UAP payloads into the secure system core.
